## 7. Common pitfalls

- **Data leakage:** splitting by frame instead of by patient/video. This is the #1 cause of fake 99% accuracy.
- **Judging only on accuracy:** always check per-class sensitivity.
- **Domain shift:** a model trained on dataset A often fails on your app's snapshots. Test on your own images early.
- **Trusting Grad-CAM as ground truth:** it shows attention, not verified lesion boundaries.
- **Hidden shortcuts:** the model may learn watermarks, instrument presence, or a specific hospital's color tone instead of pathology. Inspect heatmaps on correct predictions too.
- **Overconfident output:** show "uncertain" when confidence is low, and never present results as a diagnosis.
- **Patient privacy:** de-identify images, don't log patient info, keep inference on-premises.

